<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46047" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sub-servĭo</span></b> ,
		īre, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to be subject to</i>, <i>to serve</i> (ante-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">istaec, quae viros subservire Sibi postulant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Men. 5, 2, 14</span></i>
			; Naev. ap. <i><span class="en">Front. Ep. 2, 13, p. 62</span></i> Nieb. (Com.
			Rel. p. 22 Rib.).—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to comply with</i>,
				<i>humor</i>, <i>accommodate one's
				self to</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orationi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					And. 4, 3, 20</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
